          "anchor": "mse435-u05-c03-product-distribution-p02",
          "definition": "Nearly free per user; flat pricing prints margin.",
          "term": "software distribution"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "mse435-u05-c03-product-distribution-p04",
          "definition": "Marginal cost per token; heavy users can cost more than they pay.",
          "term": "AI distribution"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "mse435-u05-c03-product-distribution-p03",
          "definition": "p - u_i; margin per cohort.",
          "term": "margin"
        }
      ],
      "minutes": 4,
      "recall": [
        {
          "anchor": "mse435-u05-c03-product-distribution-p03",
          "answer": "Software's marginal cost is zero, so flat pricing prints margin. AI's marginal cost is per token: heavy users can cost more than they pay, so flat pricing subsidizes them.",
          "id": "mse435-u05-c03-product-distribution-r1",
          "question": "Why does flat pricing break for AI?"
        }
      ],
      "title": "mse435-U05-C03 , product distribution"
    },
    {
